From e6bd94661e6cc189b7221eb59a04abb6193ecc69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "F. Duncanh" <fduncanh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 21:28:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 35/43] Extensive NTP rewrite, to work with kernel timestamps

Now carry out all NTP statistics calculations in doubles.
to avoid confusion between NTP timestamps (Q32.32 format)
and seconds  Add -d code to explictly show that NTP is working.
Windows kernel timestamp code is now verified, and works
(if "Software Timestamp" NetAdapterAdvanceProperty has been enabled
as "RxAll" by the Windows SysAdmin).  Linux/MacOS/*BSD Posix
kernel timestamps just work "out of the box".

(cherry picked from commit 4bfa59463082a8f172fdde7aba00fc4ced74da8a)
